==Norwegian Bokmål==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|nb|fr|accord}}, derived from {{m|fr|accorder}}, from {{der|nb|LL.|accordare||to make agree}}.

===Noun===
{{nb-noun-m1}}

# a [[debt settlement]], [[composition]], [[arrangement]]; an arrangement between a [[creditor]] and his/her [[debtor]] aiming to spare the latter from [[bankruptcy]]. Also used in the sense of [[compromise]].
#: {{ux|nb|De måtte søke om '''akkord.'''|They had to apply for a '''debt settlement'''.}}
# a [[piece work]] contract, [[piece rate]]; a work where one is paid according to his/her performance rather than the number of hours.
#: {{ux|nb|De ansatte arbeider på '''akkord'''.|The employees are on '''piecework'''.}}
# {{lb|nb|music}} a [[chord]]; combination of and harmony between three or more pitches.
#: {{ux|nb|Hun slo an en '''akkord''' på pianoet.|She struck a '''chord''' on the piano.}}

====Synonyms====
* (''a settlement, arrangement'') {{l|nb|avtale}}, {{l|nb|forlik}}, {{l|nb|overenskomst}}
* (''a chord'') {{l|nb|samklang}}, {{l|nb|harmoni}}, {{l|nb|klang}}

====Derived terms====
{{der-top}}
* {{l|nb|akkordens ånd}}
* {{l|nb|frivillig akkord}}
* {{l|nb|gå på akkord med}}
* {{l|nb|offentlig akkord}}
{{der-bottom}}

